 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Action completed before name",
   "texto": [
    "In verbs, **-(으)ㄴ** before a name usually presents the action as finished: hhhhh → **본 영화** (the film I saw), hhhhh → **먹은 음식** (the food I ate), hhhhh → **만난 친구** (the friend I met). The form of the subordinate does not in itself set the time of all the prayer; the context clarifies it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "How it forms",
   "texto": [
    "With verbal roots finished in vocal is added **-ㄴ**; with another consonant, **-은**: ∞ → **간 곳**, ∞ → **먹은 음식**. Las raíces en **ㄹ** pierden la ㄹ: 살다 → **산 집**, 만들다 → **만든 음식**. On the other hand, adjectives use - (h2) h2 to describe a state: **큰 집** = large house. Contra **산 집** (house where someone lived / bought, according to the verb and context) with **사는 집** (house in which they live)."
   ]
  },
